                "searchText": "Security and Trust for Decision-Makers Nodics treats authentication, authorization, tenant isolation, validation, audit, diagnostics, and recovery as platform contracts, while deployment security remains shared. Understand how Nodics approaches security and what still belongs to the adopting organization. No source-code knowledge is required. Nodics security capabilities Evaluate Nodics Built into the platform model Separated employee, customer, internal-service, and scheduled access paths. Route-level authentication and permission metadata. Tenant-aware data and runtime context. Governed configuration changes with approval, audit, and rollback where supported. Safe diagnostics and tests for rejected and boundary behavior. Shared responsibility Nodics cannot secure an unsafe deployment automatically. Partners and operators remain responsible for infrastructure, network boundaries, credentials, provider hardening, patches, backup, monitoring, permissions, and project-specific code. Evidence to request Threat model and authority boundaries. Authentication and authorization contract tests. Tenant-isolation and ownership tests. Secret-handling, audit, recovery, and incident procedures. Deployment-specific exposure and readiness configuration."
