                "searchText": "Set Up Nodics Locally Use the repository runtime versions, install deterministically, build generated artifacts, run baseline tests, and start an explicitly selected local server. Prepare and verify a local Nodics development runtime. Basic terminal, Git, Node.js, and database familiarity. Nodics development tooling Get Started Prerequisites Git and a supported terminal. Node.js 24.18.0 is the repository-pinned version; the package accepts Node.js 22 through 26. npm 10 or 11. The database and optional providers required by the selected local topology. Install and build Start an explicit runtime Choose the environment and server intentionally. For current BackOffice-oriented local work, the consolidated runtime is the startioLocal monoServer. If a server name exists in several environments and the terminal is interactive, Nodics prompts for the environment. Automation must supply an unambiguous environment instead of depending on a prompt. Verify success The process reports the selected environment and server. Required modules become ready without repeated core-data creation. Focused baseline tests remain green. No unexpected generated or configuration files appear in Git status."
