                "depth": "implementation",
                "summary": "Nodics loads selected module configuration in deterministic order, merges eligible layered values, validates contracts, and starts services only after their required context is available.",
                "searchText": "Configuration Resolution and Runtime Behavior Nodics loads selected module configuration in deterministic order, merges eligible layered values, validates contracts, and starts services only after their required context is available. Understand how configuration becomes effective and how runtime changes remain governed. Read Nodics Configuration Layer. Nodics configuration and runtime-governance capabilities Platform Capabilities Startup sequence Resolve the selected environment and server or node topology. Discover module groups and modules belonging to that topology. Load framework defaults before more specific project and deployment layers. Merge supported objects using the framework configuration contract. Initialize classes, schemas, services, routes, pipelines, events, and module lifecycle hooks. Declare readiness only when required startup work has completed; optional integrations recover asynchronously according to their resilience policy. Scope and precedence A more specific layer may refine a supported value while the reusable module remains authoritative for its default and contract. Environment, server, node, tenant, and customer scope are distinct concerns; the effective value must be explainable from the selected runtime context. Governed runtime changes Preview validates shape, policy, dependencies, and impact without activation. Approval records the intended change and authorized decision. Activation applies only a supported runtime configuration contract. Audit retains previous and next snapshots and actor context. Rollback restores a known prior state through the same governed boundary."
