                "searchText": "Layered Architecture Technical Reference The technical hierarchy is consistent across modules even when a small module does not require every optional layer. Map a technical artifact to its responsibility and validation expectations. Read the layered architecture pages. Nodics modular runtime and all module owners Reference Artifact map config: properties, definitions, presets, and lifecycle scripts. src/schema and src/search: governed data and query contracts. src/service and src/facade: owned behavior and use-case coordination. src/controller and src/router: transport adaptation and API declarations. src/pipelines and src/interceptors: ordered processing and explicit lifecycle extensions. src/event: event declarations, listeners, and handlers. src/lib and src/utils: narrow reusable mechanics. src/status: stable success and error definitions. test: focused contracts plus integration and regression evidence. Dependency direction Higher-level use-case and transport layers depend on owned services and contracts. Provider adapters implement provider-neutral framework contracts. Business modules do not reach around those contracts to bind directly to infrastructure clients."
