            "searchText": "Pipelines and Interceptors Pipelines coordinate bounded technical steps; interceptors extend declared lifecycle points; durable business processes belong to workflow modules. Understand configurable ordered execution and explicit lifecycle extension points. Know services and the operation lifecycle. Nodics pipeline engine and each capability's pipeline definitions Platform Capabilities When to use what Use a service for small cohesive behavior. Use a pipeline when ordered replaceable steps, shared context, and error traceability are part of the contract. Use an interceptor to add behavior at a declared lifecycle point. Use workflow for durable business state, waiting, human and automatic actions, retries across time, and business-visible lifecycle. Value Customize a step without copying the entire operation. Make order, context, success, failure, and diagnostics explicit. Reuse save, search, import, job, and governance execution patterns. Trace failures to pipeline, instance, node, module, tenant, and safe cause. Continue [Pipeline Runtime and Safe Extension](/docs/capabilities/execution-processes/runtime) [Pipeline and Interceptor Technical Reference](/docs/reference/execution-processes)",
