                "searchText": "Design and Extend Shared Helpers A shared helper has explicit inputs, outputs, side effects, errors, performance, security, compatibility, consumers, and override rules. Create a stable helper without hiding dependencies or ownership. Know all current and intended consumers. Specific capability or nCommon Build and Extend Implementation sequence Search for an existing helper and owning capability. Prove several framework consumers and no clearer owner before using nCommon. Prefer a pure deterministic function; pass required context explicitly. Avoid network, filesystem, provider, database, secret, or mutable-global behavior in a general utility. Document compatibility and layer overrides; never monkey-patch globals. Test invalid input, boundaries, error cause propagation, concurrency where relevant, and all critical consumers. Security and performance Never add secret-bearing convenience serialization or logging. Keep high-volume helpers bounded and allocation-aware. Preserve original safe cause, correlation, module, tenant, and execution layer. Measure widely used helpers before adding expensive abstraction."
