            "searchText": "Schema Composition and Runtime Models Nodics composes schema definitions at runtime, supplies the base contract where appropriate, and creates models that interact through provider-neutral data services. Understand inheritance, layered merging, model generation, and provider delegation. Read Schema and Item Modeling. Nodics schema, data-model, and database capabilities Platform Capabilities Composition The owning module declares its schema-specific properties and policies. Framework base properties are composed at runtime; a schema should not repeat inherited declarations merely to imitate generated output. A layered project module may refine supported properties without replacing the original authority. The effective schema is validated before the runtime model becomes available. Runtime model behavior Resolve tenant and module context. Load the effective schema and provider configuration. Apply authorization, validation, interceptors, lifecycle rules, and transaction policy. Delegate persistence to the configured database model handler. Trigger configured cache, search, event, audit, or versioning behavior through their owned contracts. Optional capabilities Search, caching, versioning, publishing, and workflow are enabled per owning module or schema according to configuration. Their metadata must not imply that every record automatically uses every capability.",
