                "searchText": "Operate and Secure Persistence Production persistence needs provider-qualified encryption, credentials, capacity, indexing, backup, recovery, failover, and tenant isolation. Secure, monitor, tune, recover, and qualify persistence. Know the data topology and selected provider. Deployment operators and selected database provider Deploy and Operate Secure Use authenticated encrypted connections and least-privilege credentials. Keep secrets in governed secret layers and rotate them safely. Enforce schema read/write and field policy before provider calls. Prevent cross-tenant connection, model, cache, log, and backup leakage. Monitor Connection and pool health, saturation, wait time, and reconnects. Operation latency, throughput, conflicts, timeouts, and errors. Slow queries, scans, index use, storage growth, and transaction outcomes. Tenant-safe dimensions, backup freshness, replication lag, and restore evidence. Recover and qualify Test startup without the provider and mid-operation outage. Prove reconnect, retry limits, idempotency, transaction rollback, and cleanup. Exercise backup, point-in-time or supported restore, failover, schema migration, rollback, and version upgrade. Load-test realistic query shapes and isolation; a local happy-path test is insufficient."
