            "searchText": "Events and Messaging Technical Reference Each event defines its owner, stable type/version, context, delivery model, consumer behavior, failure policy, observability, and compatibility contract. Audit event ownership, delivery contracts, providers, and verification. Read the events and messaging journey. Framework event, EMS provider, and NEMS distribution contracts Reference Event checklist Owner, name, version, active state, source, target, tenant, trace, and schema. Publication point and authoritative state transition. Local, transported, persisted, replayable, or best-effort delivery. Ordering, acknowledgement, idempotency, retry, dead/failed state, and recovery. Payload minimization, authorization, retention, masking, and compatibility. Provider checklist Connection, destinations, serialization, acknowledgement, redelivery, ordering, batching, backpressure, and limits. Readiness, reconnect, failover, diagnostics, drain, and close. Positive, negative, boundary, contract, integration, load, failure, security, recovery, upgrade, and regression tests.",
