                "searchText": "Build Data Source and Destination Providers Providers resolve named configuration, stage or deliver bounded data, and return normalized evidence; they never accept arbitrary request credentials or bypass the shared lifecycle. Integrate SFTP, object storage, HTTPS, partner APIs, enterprise gateways, or delivery systems safely. Know the import remote-source or export destination contract. Reusable provider or customer-project adapter module Build and Extend Import source provider Register named sources and transports in layered configuration. Resolve credentials through secret governance. Enforce tenant/module allowlists, timeouts, retries, count, size, extension, and checksum policy. Stage files into an isolated server-owned location. Return trusted references to the normal import lifecycle and clean up according to policy. Export destination provider Register governed destination aliases and capabilities. Accept normalized streams or batches from the shared export engine. Enforce path/key constraints, encryption, checksums, retries, idempotency, retention, and cleanup. Return normalized delivery evidence without exposing provider secrets. Qualification Invalid configuration and secret handling. Tenant isolation and source/destination authorization. Timeout, retry, duplicate, partial transfer, resume, cleanup, and shutdown. Live provider compatibility, limits, performance, outage, recovery, security, and upgrade."
