                "depth": "implementation",
                "summary": "Publication requests move through staged, validation, approval, activation, online, failure, and rollback states with optimistic revision and immutable transition evidence.",
                "searchText": "Publishing Lifecycle, Rollback, and Operations Publication requests move through staged, validation, approval, activation, online, failure, and rollback states with optimistic revision and immutable transition evidence. Configure, execute, observe, and recover publication. Know the domain adapter, workflow, versions, dependencies, and Online target. nPublish lifecycle plus owning workflow, version, domain, and deployment providers Deploy and Operate Governed lifecycle Create request for exact tenant, domain, items, versions, and target. Validate source state, dependencies, manifest, target readiness, and authorization. Obtain workflow decision without duplicating workflow state. Activate through the configured domain and target adapters. Record atomic journal and query-oriented audit projection. Reconcile missing projections and refresh derived cache/search/export behavior. Rollback through an auditable previous-version deployment where supported. Failure boundaries Optimistic revision and idempotent terminal replay prevent accidental duplicate transitions. Target timeout may leave unknown completion; reconcile before retry. External effects require business compensation; database rollback alone is insufficient. Never bypass target transport, write Online storage directly, or publish an unapproved mutable record. Evidence Stage, validate, approve/reject, activate, visible online, cache/search refresh, duplicate, stale revision, dependency failure, target outage, retry, reconciliation, rollback, tenant isolation, security, performance, integration, and regression tests."
