                "summary": "Product owns stable product identity, variants, categories, attributes, catalog relationships, merchandising data, and product-specific validation—not price balances or warehouse stock.",
                "searchText": "Product Catalog Product owns stable product identity, variants, categories, attributes, catalog relationships, merchandising data, and product-specific validation—not price balances or warehouse stock. Model and publish product information independently from price and stock. Understand catalogs, schemas, workflows, and publishing. Product capability Platform Capabilities Model Stable product and variant identity. Categories, classifications, attributes, media references, units, relationships, bundles, and lifecycle. Flexible types including physical goods, services, digital items, land, real-estate, and agricultural assets through extensible schemas. Catalog and version context without duplicating CMS, Pricing, Inventory, or Units authority. Staged to Online Business users edit versioned staged products where enabled. A workflow associates exact changed versions and performs manual/automatic validation and approval. nPublish uses the Product-owned dependency, manifest, and target adapter contracts. Online stores the approved deployed form without authoring/version behavior. Search and cache refresh through existing contracts after successful publication."
