            "searchText": "Use Units and Land Measurements Define stable units, compatible dimensions, canonical conversion, precision, and rounding before using them in Product or Inventory. Configure measured products and stock without mixing dimensions. Know the product and inventory measurement requirements. Units owns definitions/conversions; consuming modules own business meaning Platform Capabilities Examples Count: each, pack, case. Mass: kilogram, gram, tonne. Volume: litre, millilitre. Area: square metre, hectare, acre and configured land units. Length and other dimensions only through compatible definitions. Implementation Choose dimension, code, symbol, canonical unit, conversion factor, precision, and rounding. Preserve original value/unit for audit and normalize only through Units services. Reject incompatible conversions such as kilograms to litres without a domain-owned density rule. Test zero, fractional, maximum precision, rounding, conversion chains, locale display, and regression.",
