                "searchText": "AI Technical Reference Every AI feature declares authority, configuration, identity, data, model/provider, budgets, tools, approval, lifecycle, observability, failure, and release evidence. Audit AI providers, economics, knowledge, assistants, tools, recovery, and verification. Read the AI capability journey. Nodics AI modules and every invoked capability owner Reference Checklist Usage profile, provider capabilities, model, reviewed pricing, secret reference, timeout, cancellation, fallback, rate, circuit, and kill switch. Tenant, enterprise, project, user, conversation, operation budgets, reservation, ledger, reconciliation, and retention. Corpus/source ownership, schema/service read contract, chunking, embedding, search mode, version, freshness, permission, evidence, and citation. Assistant definition, approved prompt, context/redaction, conversation ownership, SSE events, leases, cancellation, recovery, tools, confirmation, and Workflow handoff. No direct database/search/provider/tool authority bypass. Positive, negative, boundary, contract, integration, concurrency, prompt-injection, authorization, cost, load, outage, recovery, live-provider, security, and regression tests."
