                "searchText": "Search Models and Querying Search models describe searchable behavior and normalized operations; configured providers execute engine-specific indexing and queries. Understand how Nodics exposes searchable business data without coupling callers to one search engine. Understand the purpose of a Nodics schema and item model. Nodics provider-neutral search capability Platform Capabilities Four different responsibilities The owning business schema defines authoritative records and business rules. A source-owned index definition declares what should be searchable. The provider-neutral search model exposes normalized index and query operations. A configured engine adapter translates those operations to an external engine. Why this separation matters Business modules should not contain Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, or Solr client calls. They declare searchable intent and call the shared search contract, allowing the engine to change without rewriting business callers. Continue Learn how search models work Define searchable data Explore search providers"
