                "searchText": "Prebuilt Search Engines The generic search module is the caller contract; Elasticsearch is the current engine-specific adapter. Select and qualify an available Nodics search implementation. Understand the provider-neutral search contract. gFramework/nSearch Platform Capabilities Provider-neutral search Owns secured schema and index routes. Owns normalized models, pipelines, errors, cache policy, and fallback rules. Must remain free of engine client calls and customer index topology. Elasticsearch adapter Owns connection handling, raw Elastic search-model loading, operation mapping, and client calls. Supports health, refresh, exists, get, search, save, bulk, update, remove, remove by query, schema, and index lifecycle operations. Normalizes the historical hosts configuration to the client nodes option. Is guarded: deterministic tests exist, but each production deployment requires live cluster, security, version, recovery, and performance qualification. Configuration boundary Endpoints, credentials, index names, aliases, tenant routing, timeouts, retries, refresh, mappings, and engine topology belong to layered configuration or approved secret/runtime governance—not provider-neutral business source."
